/*
 * Cross-origin isolation — required for SharedArrayBuffer / high-resolution
 * timers used by some features of ya-webadb. Without these headers, scrcpy
 * video decoding and framebuffer capture won't work.
 *
 * Cloudflare Pages serves these on every response in the project, including
 * static HTML, JS chunks, and worker invocations.
 *
 * Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
 *   Tells the browser this page may only embed resources that explicitly
 *   opt-in via CORP (same-origin, same-site, or cross-origin).
 *
 * Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
 *   Isolates the browsing context group from other origins. Combined with
 *   COEP, this unlocks `crossOriginIsolated === true` in JS.
 *
 * Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
 *   Allows same-origin pages (e.g. /_next chunks) to be embedded without
 *   needing every third-party CDN to set CORP. Since webadb.online has no
 *   third-party assets (everything is bundled), same-origin is the strictest
 *   safe choice.
 */

/
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Long-cache hashed assets — Next.js generates content-hashed filenames so
# they can be cached forever.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Don't cache HTML — it changes per-deploy.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Security headers, applied globally.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: usb=(self)